hived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-08-19T09:02:50Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T09:07:25Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproduced in `4.8.dev`[944a3c6], `4.7.stable`.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1088) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-12700H (20 threads) - 15.69 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nRelated issue:\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122584\n\nNot sure if this is a bug, but it does feel inconsistent.\n\nA named enum key's tooltip does not show the constant value when used. However, an unnamed enum key's tooltip shows the constant value when used.\n\n```gdscript\n# main.gd\nextends Node\n\nenum Named {\n\tA = 10,\n}\n\nenum {\n\tB = 20,\n}\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tprint(Named.A) # has tooltips (Enumeration \"main.gd\".Named) and (Constant \"main.gd\".Named.A); \"= 10\" is missing?\n\tprint(B) # has tooltip (Constant \"main.gd\".B : @unnamed_enums = 20)\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Paste the GDScript above into the script editor.\n2. Hover the cursor over the identifiers to check the tooltips.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122585/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122585/timeline","performed_via_github_app":